{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1290532-storypath-for-cod","id":1290532,"title":"Storypath for CoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-21T14:16:27-08:00","id":1290532,"title":"Storypath for CoD","content":"I have been planning on using Storypath for Chronicles of Darkness (Vampire the Requiem, Mage the Awakening, Werewolf the Forsaken). If this plan works out then I may move on to Exalted, we will see.<br /> <br /> Some of my reasons are the number of dice a CoD splat can throw around, it becomes more about dice and less about the story. For example a BP 2 or 3 vampire using Physical Intensity and a fighting style merit to sac his defense and add it all to his attack. Not counting frenzy and other items become a game of Rollplaying instead of Roleplaying. I love the concept of Exalted however I am not a fan of the loads of dice you are throwing to make it happen.<br /> <br /> My approach will be the start with the basic character building, add on templates and then see how to make those templates work. I am open to feedback and collaborative assistance. What I am not open to is &quot;why would you do that&quot;, or &quot;that is a terrible idea&quot;, or &quot;you can't do that because&quot;.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T14:32:29-08:00","id":1290537,"title":"","content":"<b>Character Creation</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Character Concept</b><ul><li>Name</li> <li>Concept Phrase</li> <li>Template and Setting Specifics<ul><li>Mage: Supernal Path &amp; Arcane Order</li> <li>Scion: Divine Patron &amp; Genesis</li> <li>Trinity: Psi Order &amp; Aptitude</li> <li>Vampire: Clan &amp; Covenant</li> <li>Werewolf: Auspice &amp; Tribe</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Paths (3)</b><ul><li><b>Origin Path: </b>Background, life choices, formative experiences</li> <li><b>Role Path: </b>Occupation, profession, area of expertise</li> <li><b>Society Path: </b>Debts, factions, groups, organization, relationships<ul><li><b>Setting Specific</b><ul><li>Allegiances (Psions)</li> <li>Supernal Path &amp; Arcane Order (Mage)</li> <li>Auspice &amp; Tribe (Werewolf)</li> <li>Clan &amp; Covenant (Vampire)</li> <li>Pantheons (Scions)</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Select three Skills per path (with storyguide approval)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Skills (18)</b><ul><li>Prioritize your Paths as primary, secondary, and tertiary</li> <li>Path Skills each receive \u2026<ul><li><b>Primary</b>: 3 dots (max 5 dots)</li> <li><b>Secondary</b>: 2 dots (max 5 dots)</li> <li><b>Tertiary</b>: 1 dots (max 5 dots)</li> </ul></li> <li>These dots are cumulative for Skills associated with multiple paths.</li> <li>Any Skill over 5 dots must be redistributed to another Path Skill</li> <li><b>Specialties: </b>Pick a specialty for any Skills at 3 dots or more</li> <li><b>Skill Tricks:</b> (Trinity)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Attributes (21)</b><ul><li>Each of the nine Attributes starts at 1 dot</li> <li>Prioritize your Attribute Arenas (Mental, Physical, and Social) as primary, secondary, and tertiary.</li> <li>Distribute points among your Attribute Arena<ul><li><b>Primary</b>: 5 dots</li> <li><b>Secondary</b>: 4 dots</li> <li><b>Tertiary</b>: 3 dots</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Variant Scion</b>: Distribute points among your Attribute Arena<ul><li><b>Primary</b>: 6 dots</li> <li><b>Secondary</b>: 4 dots</li> <li><b>Tertiary</b>: 2 dots\u200b</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Apply Template</b><ul><li>See Template Sections</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Edges (Merits)</b><ul><li>You may gain access to unique Edges (Merits) based on your Template</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Finishing Touches</b><ul><li><b>Bonus Traits</b><ul><li>Apply 5 extra Skill dots</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Defense</b></li> <li><b>Health</b></li> <li><b>Integrity?</b></li> <li><b>Speed: </b>2x Athletics Dice Pool in meters ?</li> <li><b>Aspirations (Deeds)</b><ul><li>Long Term (1): Path goals across arcs representing growth and change</li> <li>Short Term (2): Goals within an Episode or Session</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 02-25-2019, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T14:34:20-08:00","id":1290538,"title":"","content":"Ok here is my base character creation using a combination of CoD and Storypath. Please give feedback and let me know what you think I have in error or missing. I have some VtR, WtF, and MtA items I will post once we iron out some of this.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T23:47:08-08:00","id":1290666,"title":"","content":"Myself, I using elements of <b>Storypath</b> in our <b>Werewolf</b> game - like 'first decide Skill' and 'use Milestones in Extended Actions' - just to test waters before our planned <b>Scion</b> game, later this year. It work good for now. But I did not use complex new <b>Storypath</b> mechanics - like Complications or Enchantments. Have idea how this two would translate, in context of <b>CoD</b> mechanics using those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T03:03:52-08:00","id":1290703,"title":"","content":"Jumping to to number 7 where some of my CoD / SP start to divert.<br /> * Bonus Attribute: Can anyone tell me is it Scion and Trinity? Makes sense for VtR Clan Attribute, MtA Resilience Attribute, WtF does not get a free Attribute so we need to consider if we want to give one based on Auspice maybe to bring them in line.<br /> * Do mortals of Trinity/Scion gain this free Attribute? I was hoping to list it in the Template section for each VtR, MtA, WtF, Scion, Trinity.<br /> * Maybe mortal gets its own Template/Un-Template.<br /> * Defense as SP, even though I have not yet embraced it. <br /> * Health as SP, will be extra work moving for Templates, Powers/Disciplines/Gifts etc. <br /> * Speed will be range bands as in SP which was already in the works with Hurt Locker/Exalted. Formula if something specific is needed.<br /> * Aspirations/Deeds are easy as SP. <br /> * Integrity is going to be an immediate challenge as it ties deeply into every splat of CoD and in so many different ways. <br /> * I prefer the MtA three tiers approach and started using this for VtR and WtF. Really appreciate any feedback and ideas on making this SP friendly. <br /> * What else? Feedback?<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T07:43:50-08:00","id":1290756,"title":"","content":"I figure with Integrity (Humanity, Harmony, Wisdom, Clarity, ...) I have a few options <br /> <br /> 1. Use the CoD as is, least desirable. <br /> 2. Use SP Integrity Skill, I don't think that will play to the multi-splat importance. <br /> 3. Something new, blend of MtA three tiers, and SP simplicity. Maybe a scales of 1-5 ,1 being the worst and 5 a saint. Maybe the CoD 0-10 can flatten to a new 0-5 or 1-5.<br /> <br /> Feedback welcome<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T19:07:08-08:00","id":1292677,"title":"","content":"So here is how VtR2's Humanity is scaled. <br /> <br /> <br /> Here's how the chart works. If your Humanity is greater than or equal to where the breaking point is listed, you make a Detachment check. Roll the number of dice in the parenthesis, and if you even score one success, you don't lose Humanity. These are several ways to gain bonuses and penalties to Detachment checks, with the most important being touchstones. <br /> <br /> Humanity 10 (Five Dice)<br /> \u2022 One night without human contact.<br /> \u2022 Lying in defense of the Masquerade.<br /> \u2022 Spending more than one Vitae in a night.<br /> <br /> Humanity 9 (Five Dice)<br /> \u2022 Watching humans eat a meal. <br /> \u2022 Committing a superhuman feat of physical prowess. <br /> \u2022 Feeding from the unwilling or unknowing. <br /> \u2022 Urging another\u2019s behavior with a Discipline. <br /> \u2022 Spending an hour in the sun. <br /> <br /> Humanity 8 (Four Dice)<br /> \u2022 Creating a ghoul. <br /> \u2022 Rejected by a human. <br /> \u2022 Riding the wave of frenzy. <br /> \u2022 Depriving another of consent with a Discipline.<br /> \u2022 Spending most of a day in the sun. <br /> <br /> Humanity 7 (Four Dice)<br /> \u2022 One week active without human contact. <br /> \u2022 Surviving something that would hospitalize a human. <br /> \u2022 Injuring someone over blood. <br /> <br /> Humanity 6 (Three Dice)<br /> \u2022 Falling into torpor. <br /> \u2022 Feeding from a child. <br /> \u2022 Reading your own obituary. <br /> \u2022 Experiencing a car crash or other immense physical trauma.<br /> <br /> Humanity 5 (Three Dice)<br /> \u2022 Two weeks active without human contact.<br /> \u2022 Reaching Blood Potency 3.<br /> \u2022 Death of a mortal family member.<br /> \u2022 Joining a covenant to the point of gaining Status for it. <br /> <br /> Humanity 4 (Two Dice)<br /> \u2022 Learning a dot of Cr\u00faac.<br /> \u2022 Impassioned violence.<br /> \u2022 Spending a year or more in torpor.<br /> \u2022 Surviving a century.<br /> \u2022 Accidentally killing. <br /> <br /> Humanity 3 (Two Dice)<br /> \u2022 One month active without human contact.<br /> \u2022 Reaching Blood Potency 6.<br /> \u2022 Death of a mortal spouse or child.<br /> \u2022 Impassioned killing. <br /> <br /> Humanity 2 (One Die)<br /> \u2022 One year active without human contact.<br /> \u2022 Premeditated killing.<br /> \u2022 Seeing a culture that didn\u2019t exist when you were alive.<br /> \u2022 Surviving 500 years.<br /> \u2022 Creating a revenant. <br /> <br /> Humanity 1 (Zero Dice)<br /> \u2022 One decade active without human contact.<br /> \u2022 Heinous, spree, or mass murder.<br /> \u2022 Killing your Touchstone. <br /> <br /> Zero dice means rolling a chance die. A chance die, in Masquerade terms, is a dice pool of 1 at difficulty 10. Rolling a 1 on a chance die results in a Dramatic Failure (or botch in Masquerade).<br /> <br /> A Touchstone is someone or something that means something to a vampire, and reminds him of his Humanity. In game terms, Touchstones provide bonuses to Detachment rolls. They can also talk a vampire out of Frenzy much easier than other characters. Several Conditions (status effects) can be mitigated or even removed by spending some quality time with your Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Other Breaking Points<br /> <br /> Diablerie is not included in the chart in the book, but was confirmed to be a Humanity 1 breaking point by the developers. It is no longer an automatic Humanity loss. However, creating a new vampire now results in an automatic Humanity loss.<br /> <br /> Integrity System<br /> <br /> All splats in the CoD have an Integrity system. <br /> \u2022 Mortals/Hunters - Morality (1e)/Integrity (2e)<br /> \u2022 Vampires - Humanity<br /> \u2022 Mages - Wisdom<br /> \u2022 Werewolf - Harmony<br /> \u2022 Prometheans - Humanity<br /> \u2022 Changelings - Clarity<br /> \u2022 Sin-Eaters - Synergy<br /> \u2022 Mummies - Memory<br /> \u2022 Demons - Cover<br /> \u2022 Beasts - Satiety","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T08:37:25-08:00","id":1292774,"title":"","content":"There are minor Social modifiers listed. These modifiers apply to rolls relating to humans. Manipulating humans for food with Subterfuge or frightening them with Intimidation are not affected; but trying to understand a human\u2019s emotional cues with the Empathy Skill would be affected.<br /> <br /> Humanity Scale<br /> \u2022 Ascetic (Humanity 9-10) (Social +2d)<br /> \u2022 Humane (Humanity 7-8)<br /> \u2022 Balanced (Humanity 5-6) (Social -1d)<br /> \u2022 Weathered (Humanity 4) (Social -2d)<br /> \u2022 Callous (Humanity 3) (Social -3d)<br /> \u2022 Monstrous (Humanity 2) (Social -5d)<br /> \u2022 Animalistic (Humanity 1) ,(Social Chance Die)<br /> \u2022 Draugr (Humanity 0) (Social NA)<br /> <br /> Best Regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T08:45:56-08:00","id":1292778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1290532-storypath-for-cod?p=1292774#post1292774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are minor Social modifiers listed. These modifiers apply to rolls relating to humans. Manipulating humans for food with Subterfuge or frightening them with Intimidation are not affected; but trying to understand a human\u2019s emotional cues with the Empathy Skill would be affected.<br /> <br /> Humanity Scale<br /> \u2022 Ascetic (Humanity 9-10) (Social +2d)<br /> \u2022 Humane (Humanity 7-8)<br /> \u2022 Balanced (Humanity 5-6) (Social -1d)<br /> \u2022 Weathered (Humanity 4) (Social -2d)<br /> \u2022 Callous (Humanity 3) (Social -3d)<br /> \u2022 Monstrous (Humanity 2) (Social -5d)<br /> \u2022 Animalistic (Humanity 1) ,(Social Chance Die)<br /> \u2022 Draugr (Humanity 0) (Social NA)<br /> <br /> Best Regards</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the revised MtA/Storypath version I would start to work with is as follows.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity Scale (0-5)<br /> \u2022 Ascetic (Humanity 5) (5d | Social +2e)<br /> \u2022 Balanced (Humanity 4) (4d | default new vampire)<br /> \u2022 Weathered (Humanity 3) (3d | Social +1c)<br /> \u2022 Callous (Humanity 2) (2d | Social +2c)<br /> \u2022 Monstrous (Humanity 1) (1d | Social +3c)<br /> \u2022 Lost (Humanity 0) (Social NA)<br /> <br /> Touchstones<br /> One (+1e)<br /> More (+2e)<br /> <br /> Level of Breaking Point<br /> 5 (+0) (previously 9-10)<br /> 4 (+1) (previously 7-8)<br /> 3 (+2) (previously 5-6)<br /> 2 (+3) (previously 3-4)<br /> 1 (+4) (previously 1-2)<br /> <br /> Difficulty = 1 + Breaking Point mod above<br /> <br /> Ok that was off the cuff, now I will consider, review the mortal breaking points as I think they will weave in easily.<br /> <br /> Any feedback is welcome<br /> <br /> Notes: 2-3d = 1 change in diffculty or +1 enhancement (rough CoD to SP conversion)<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 02-28-2019, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T09:43:10-08:00","id":1292793,"title":"","content":"So example time<br /> <br /> New vampire Humanity 4 and one touchstone.<br /> * 4d +1e for detachment rolls<br /> <br /> Vampire frenzies from hunger and accidentally kills during feeding.<br /> * New = Breaking Point 2 = difficulty 4 (1 + 3 difficulty) [4% success - opps]<br /> * VtR = Breaking Point 4 = 4d (2d + 2d touchstone) [77% success]<br /> <br /> Vampire walks away from a car crash<br /> * New = Breaking Point 3 = difficulty 3 (1 + 2 difficulty) [17% success - opps]<br /> * VtR = Breaking Point 6 = 5d (3d + 2d touchstone) [84% success]<br /> <br /> My knee jerk reaction is I need to drop the breaking point mod by 1 as it seems to high.<br /> Ok, ya I ran the number and time to rethink.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 02-28-2019, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T18:36:00-08:00","id":1292902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1290532-storypath-for-cod?p=1292778#post1292778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So the revised MtA/Storypath version I would start to work with is as follows.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity Scale (0-5)<br /> \u2022 Ascetic (Humanity 5) (Social +2e)<br /> \u2022 Balanced (Humanity 4) (Social +0e) <br /> default new vampire<br /> \u2022 Weathered (Humanity 3) (Social +1c)<br /> \u2022 Callous (Humanity 2) (Social +2c)<br /> \u2022 Monstrous (Humanity 1) (Social +3c)<br /> \u2022 Lost (Humanity 0) (Social NA)<br /> <br /> Touchstones<br /> One (+1e)<br /> More (+2e)<br /> <br /> Level of Breaking Point<br /> 5 (5d) (previously BP 9-10)<br /> 4 (4d) (previously BP 7-8)<br /> 3 (3d) (previously BP 5-6)<br /> 2 (2d) (previously BP 3-4)<br /> 1 (1d) (previously BP 1-2)<br /> <br /> Difficulty = 1<br /> <br /> Any feedback is welcome<br /> <br /> Notes: 2-3d = 1 change in diffculty or +1 enhancement (rough CoD to SP conversion)<br /> <br /> Best regards</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised the Breaking Point mods","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 02-28-2019, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T19:07:26-08:00","id":1292906,"title":"","content":"Ok now to rerun the example ...<br /> Ok I need to rethink this whole process I like the breaking points being 1-5 which is the number of dice to roll but what difficulty and how do touchstones help?<br /> <br /> <br /> So example time<br /> <br /> New vampire Humanity 4 and one touchstone.<br /> * +1e for detachment rolls<br /> <br /> Vampire frenzies and slaughters a biker gang<br /> * New = Breaking Point 1<br /> 1d [30% success]<br /> * VtR = Breaking Point 1<br /> 2d (0d +2 touchstone)<br /> <br /> Vampire frenzies from hunger and accidentally kills during feeding.<br /> * New = Breaking Point 2<br /> 2d<br /> * VtR = Breaking Point 4<br /> 4d (2d + 2d touchstone) [77% success]<br /> <br /> Vampire walks away from a car crash<br /> * New = Breaking Point 3<br /> 3d +1e touchstone<br /> * VtR = Breaking Point 6<br /> 5d (3d + 2d touchstone) [84% success]<br /> <br /> Vampire injures victim while feeding<br /> * New = Breaking Point 4<br /> 4d<br /> * VtR = Breaking Point 7<br /> 6d (4d + 2d touchstone)<br /> <br /> Vampire attends a dinner watching everyone eat<br /> * New = Breaking Point 5<br /> No need to roll as it's above the vampires humanity<br /> * VtR = Breaking Point 9<br /> No need to roll as it's above the vampires humanity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 03-01-2019, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T17:10:30-08:00","id":1294235,"title":"","content":"I'm not super sure about the numbers, but thematically I think it works better. Instead of being a purely binary pass or fail now youre likely to pass but with some complications, which seems to me like what the experience narratively is what its been told as. Like yes you pull through with your humanity(or integrety or..) intact but your shaken by it. I don't think I know the storypath system well enough to be much help, but I've been trying to do the same thing for my games. Maybe after Scion comes out I can teach myself it, either way I'll be keeping a close eye on your progress. Keep up the Great work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/749-worldscoolestloser","name":"worldscoolestloser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar749_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T12:28:25-07:00","id":1296200,"title":"","content":"Here is a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1296194-one-weapon-armor-matrix\">One Weapon &amp; Armor Matrix</a> that I was using with CoD and now I need to see if it can play into Storypath and how.<br /> <br /> Would love any feedback.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T15:37:44-07:00","id":1296805,"title":"","content":"OK I am ready to post my first run at CoD to Storypath conversions. These are on the fly based off previous version I tweaked just to get a discussion going.<br /> <br /> File links are <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1C8d6z1NhnqSW1oOkNfAr3x06l7J7Cayw?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T15:40:35-07:00","id":1296806,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>CoD to Storypath</b></div> <br /> <b>Weapon Maximum Range Bands</b><br /> <br /> <b>Close</b> (2m | 5ft)<ul><li><b>Close Combat Skill | +1 DR @ Close Range</b></li> <li>Unarmed</li> <li>Melee &amp; Reach</li> </ul><br /> <b>Short</b> (30m | 100ft)<ul><li><b>Aim/Firearms or Athletics Skill | +1 DR @ Close Range</b></li> <li>Civilian Flame Throwers</li> <li>Shotguns, Sawed Off Shotgun</li> <li>Sonic Pistols, Taser Pistols, Web Emitter</li> <li>Plasma Pistol, Plasma Rifle, Plasma Thrower Heavy Weapon</li> <li>Thrown Weapon (Grenade)</li> <li>Hand Crossbow</li> </ul><br /> <b>Medium</b> (100m | 300ft)<ul><li><b>Aim/Firearms Skill | +1 DR @ Close Range</b></li> <li>Pistol, Revolver, Slug Thrower</li> <li>Submachine Gun</li> <li>Grenade Launcher (Only +1 DR @ Long)</li> <li>Military Flame Thrower</li> <li>Flechette Pistol, Flechette Carbine</li> <li>Mini Laser Guantlet</li> <li>Heavy Plasma Weapon</li> <li>Short Bow, Light Crosbow</li> <li>Longbow, Heavy Crossbow (Only +1 DR @ Long)</li> </ul><br /> <b>Long</b> (1000m | 3000ft)<ul><li><b>Aim/Firearms Skill | +1 DR @ Close &amp; Short Range</b></li> <li>Assault Rifle</li> <li>Rifles, Slug Thrower Rifle</li> <li>Laser Carbine</li> <li>Heavy Coilgun</li> <li>Light Artillery</li> <li>Laser Guantlet</li> </ul><br /> <b>Extreme</b> (1001m+, 3001ft+)<ul><li>Heavy Weapons (Embanked Weapons)</li> <li>Vehicle Weapons</li> </ul><br /> <b>Out of Range</b><ul><li>+2 DR per range band beyond the weapons maximum.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T15:41:32-07:00","id":1296807,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>CoD to Storypath</b></div> <br /> Please note that I have never found a grapple system that I enjoy as both a player and GM. They range from D&amp;D 3.5 &amp; EX3 (Overly complicated), to D&amp;D 5.0 (Vanilla Bland), to Trinity 1E &amp; CoD (Almost there but whats with changing initiative \u2013 oh my head hurts). So here is hoping that Storypath becomes the one! Does anyone have any grapple systems that they really enjoy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>GRAPPLE</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Declare a Grapple Maneuver (Instant)</b><ul><li>See Grapple Maneuvers below</li> </ul><br /> <b>Start a Grapple (+1DR)</b><ul><li>Usually Dex + Close Combat vs Defense</li> <li>One hand free is required</li> <li>Extra successes add to the Control Roll</li> </ul><br /> <b>Opposed Control Roll</b><ul><li>Str + Close Combat</li> <li>Active Player (Attacker)<ul><li>Wins (Maneuver success with extra successes)</li> <li>Ties (Both grapplers struggle with no result)</li> <li>Loses (Defender escapes reflexively on his next turn)</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b>Grappling Condition</b><ul><li>While grappling both characters suffer \u2026<ul><li>Defense -2 vs other attackers</li> <li>Cannot use Mixed Actions</li> <li>Weapon attacks in a grapple suffer size as a penalty (CoD Size) ??</li> <li>No movement without the drag maneuver</li> <li>External attacks may force a new control roll</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Grapple (Continue a grapple)</b><ul><li>Break Free, Escape, Release (reflexive)</li> <li>Control Weapon or Object<ul><li>Draw a weapon or gain control of an opponents</li> </ul></li> <li>Damage/Savage with\u2026<ul><li>Bite, Claws, or Natural Weapons</li> <li>Bite &amp; Feed (Vampires)</li> <li>Melee Weapons (Weapon Size as a penalty)</li> <li>Ranged Firearms (Weapon Size as a penalty)</li> <li>Unarmed Attacks</li> </ul></li> <li>Disarm Weapon or Object<ul><li>Must success at control weapon first</li> </ul></li> <li>Drag +1DR</li> <li>Hold in Place (Neither may apply Defense vs incoming attacks)<ul><li>Choke Hold (Merit)</li> <li>Restrain/Immobilize +1DR (Tilt)<ul><li>Apply Cuffs/Manacles +1 DR (Control + s&gt;Str)</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Hold at Bay<ul><li>Gun to head, hand over mouth, knife at neck</li> <li>Take Cover/Human Shield (Breaking Point)</li> </ul></li> <li>Reverse Grapple (Reflexive)</li> <li>Throw/Slam/Drop<ul><li>Drop Prone (both go prone, no damage, grapple ends)</li> <li>Slam (+1DR, 1B/L per success, grapple ends)</li> <li>Throw (+1DR, 1B/L per success, grapple ends, close range)</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T15:42:17-07:00","id":1296808,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>CoD to Storypath</b></div> <br /> <b>COMBAT MANEUVERS (Simple Action)</b><ul><li>Aim<ul><li>+1e</li> <li>No mixed, no move, no burstfire</li> <li>If you apply Defense you loose Aim</li> </ul></li> <li>All-Out Attack<ul><li>Defense = 1 no bump</li> <li>+1e attack</li> <li>No mixed</li> </ul></li> <li>Bite by a non-human Creature with Natural Weapons<ul><li>Example sharks, wolves, ect.</li> <li>Mortals, vampire, humanoids, must grapple to bite</li> </ul></li> <li>Burstfire (Autofire)<ul><li>Single Shot (+0e, 1 target, 1 ammo)</li> <li>Short (+1e, 1 target, 3 ammo)</li> <li>Medium (+1e, 1-3 targets, 10 ammo)</li> <li>Long (+2e, many targets, 20 ammo)</li> <li>If multiple targets Complication = Medium +1DR, Long +2DR</li> <li>No penalty vs mobs or battle groups</li> </ul></li> <li>Charge<ul><li>Defense = 1 no bump</li> <li>x2 Move</li> <li>Attack</li> <li>No Mixed</li> </ul></li> <li>Coverfire<ul><li>Medium and Long Burst, CoD 90, too much text</li> </ul></li> <li>Dash/Double Move</li> <li>Defend Other<ul><li>Defender applies Defense in place of wards</li> </ul></li> <li>Disengage (Opposed Athletics)</li> <li>Distract</li> <li>Dodge</li> <li>Draw, Change, Pickup, Sheath, Sling, Stow<ul><li>May begin with weapon unless ambushed</li> </ul></li> <li>Drop Prone (Reaction or Action)<ul><li>Automatically fail disengage, withdraw contests</li> </ul></li> <li>Feint</li> <li>Full Defense<ul><li>+2 Def, No Flurry</li> </ul></li> <li>Gambit (No Flurry)<ul><li>Break Shield</li> <li>Break Weapon</li> <li>Disarm with Brawl (DR=Targets Close Combat Skill)</li> <li>Disarm with Weapon (DR=Targets Close Combat Skill)</li> <li>Disarm with Firearms (DR=Targets Close Combat Skill or object size)</li> <li>Grapple 1s</li> <li>Knockdown/Takedown 1s</li> <li>Sweep</li> <li>Tackle +1DR /+1 DMG</li> </ul></li> <li>Killing Blow<ul><li>Inflict the taken out (death on a lower tier)</li> <li>Avoids most mundane armor</li> <li>Breaking point</li> </ul></li> <li>Misc Action (-1 Def)</li> <li>Movement Maneuver<ul><li>Acrobatics, Climbing, Jumping</li> </ul></li> <li>Pulling Blow, Pommel, Flat, Hilt</li> <li>Reload</li> <li>Rise from Prone/Stand<ul><li>Opposed Athletics vs Close Combat</li> </ul></li> <li>Rush<ul><li>Opposed Athletics from Short Range</li> </ul></li> <li>Stealth<ul><li>No Flurry</li> <li>If Move DR+2</li> <li>Opposed Stealth vs Awareness or Perception</li> </ul></li> <li>Take Cover (Reaction or Action)<ul><li>Light (Defense +1, Attack from +0c)</li> <li>Medium (Defense +2, Attack from +1c)</li> <li>Heavy (Defense +3, Attack from +2c)</li> <li>Full (No Line of Sight)</li> <li>Cover does not suffer Onslaught Penalty</li> </ul></li> <li>Withdraw (Complex)<ul><li>Athletics</li> <li>EX3 = DR1, Goal 10, Each Round</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T15:43:50-07:00","id":1296809,"title":"","content":"OK that is a start now to make sure there are stunt values, enhancement, complications with everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T05:17:53-07:00","id":1297215,"title":"","content":"I am terrebly sorry, but what is storypath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T22:12:04-07:00","id":1297459,"title":"","content":"<b>Storypath </b>is 'sister' (?) game engine to <b>Storytelling System</b>, on what <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> run. The both share a lot of similarities to that extent that I treat Storypath as as 'sorta 3E' of Storytelling System. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Storypath is Onyx Path Publishing in-house system, so they are not restricted in usage of it as much as they are with Storytelling engine ( that is, de facto, owned by White Wolf ). Games ( and their forums ) that run on Storypath - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity\">Trinity Continuum</a> ( various S-F ), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion\">Scion</a> ( you play descendent of god ), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire\">They </a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire\">Came From Beneath the Sea</a> ( 1950s comedic horror ) and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/dystopia-rising-evolution-kickstarter-is-now-live/\" target=\"_blank\">Dystopia Rising: Evolution</a> ( post-app with supermutants and zombies ).<br /> <br /> Here is Storypath preview - <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187949/Storypath-System-Preview\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...System-Preview</a><br /> <br /> This reddit came in depth about similarities and differences between two game systems - \u200b<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/rpg/comments/7u8zoj/storyteller_vs_storypath_system/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/rpg/comment...rypath_system/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-17-2019, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T23:00:30-07:00","id":1297464,"title":"","content":"While I disagree with the premise (more dice means &quot;rollplaying&quot; of roleplaying), this looks super interesting and you've clearly put a lot of work in it. I'm wildly unfamiliar with Storypath, but Scion has been on my To Read list for a while now. Once I'm able to dig into the system, I'll be sure to circle back and see what feedback I can give.<br /> <br /> Looks rad, though. Good work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:42:12-07:00","id":1299268,"title":"","content":"Great job overall, thanks!<br /> <br /> Have you looked into converting the magic system of Mage the Awakening to Storypath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:01:54-07:00","id":1299443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1290532-storypath-for-cod?p=1299268#post1299268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great job overall, thanks!<br /> <br /> Have you looked into converting the magic system of Mage the Awakening to Storypath?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I have, once I work out most of the base mortal items then I will tackle VtR, MtA, and WtF.<br /> <br /> For example I plan on using something similiar to Psion Power activation dice. <br /> <br /> Spellcasting Roll = (Gnosis/2 RndUp) + 1 + Arcana<br /> <br /> This sets a range of 2-6 dice similiar to Psi score plus Mode (Arcana). <br /> <br /> So Gnosis<br /> 01 = 2d + Arcana dice<br /> 02 = 2d + Arcana dice<br /> 03 = 3d + Arcana dice<br /> 04 = 3d + Arcana dice<br /> 05 = 4d + Arcana dice<br /> <br /> Tier 3 (Target Number 7, Max Attribute 6)<br /> 06 = 4d + Arcana dice<br /> 07 = 5d + Arcana dice<br /> 08 = 5d + Arcana dice<br /> <br /> Tier 3 (Target Number 7, Max Attribute 7)<br /> 09 = 6d + Arcana dice <br /> 10 = 6d + Arcana dice <br /> <br /> Yantras will be enhancements<br /> <br /> I am considering the same thing for VtR and WtF<br /> <br /> Disciplines <br /> (Blood Potency / 2 RndUp) + 1 + Discipline Dice<br /> <br /> Gifts <br /> (Primal Urge/ 2 RndUp) + 1 + Aspect or Gift Dice<br /> <br /> This would be a method similiar to Trinity or Mage. <br /> <br /> I could also use a method more similiar to Scion or Exalted, Werewolf with Attribute and Skill dropping the third set of dice from the Supernatural Stat (Gnosis, Primal Urge, Blood Potency). I like this version less. <br /> <br /> One of my thoughts is using Scale for vampire Celerity, Resilience and Vigor. Maybe vampires Physical Intensity. <br /> <br /> And I definitely want feedback. <br /> <br /> Just be warned I have never met a system I was not willing to tinker with. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 03-24-2019, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T22:01:59-07:00","id":1300767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1290532-storypath-for-cod?p=1299443#post1299443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I have, once I work out most of the base mortal items then I will tackle VtR, MtA, and WtF.<br /> <br /> For example I plan on using something similiar to Psion Power activation dice.<br /> <br /> Spellcasting Roll = (Gnosis/2 RndUp) + 1 + Arcana<br /> <br /> This sets a range of 2-6 dice similiar to Psi score plus Mode (Arcana).<br /> <br /> So Gnosis<br /> 01 = 2d + Arcana dice<br /> 02 = 2d + Arcana dice<br /> 03 = 3d + Arcana dice<br /> 04 = 3d + Arcana dice<br /> 05 = 4d + Arcana dice<br /> <br /> Tier 3 (Target Number 7, Max Attribute 6)<br /> 06 = 4d + Arcana dice<br /> 07 = 5d + Arcana dice<br /> 08 = 5d + Arcana dice<br /> <br /> Tier 3 (Target Number 7, Max Attribute 7)<br /> 09 = 6d + Arcana dice<br /> 10 = 6d + Arcana dice<br /> <br /> Yantras will be enhancements<br /> <br /> I am considering the same thing for VtR and WtF<br /> <br /> Disciplines<br /> (Blood Potency / 2 RndUp) + 1 + Discipline Dice<br /> <br /> Gifts<br /> (Primal Urge/ 2 RndUp) + 1 + Aspect or Gift Dice<br /> <br /> This would be a method similiar to Trinity or Mage.<br /> <br /> I could also use a method more similiar to Scion or Exalted, Werewolf with Attribute and Skill dropping the third set of dice from the Supernatural Stat (Gnosis, Primal Urge, Blood Potency). I like this version less.<br /> <br /> One of my thoughts is using Scale for vampire Celerity, Resilience and Vigor. Maybe vampires Physical Intensity.<br /> <br /> And I definitely want feedback.<br /> <br /> Just be warned I have never met a system I was not willing to tinker with.<br /> <br /> Best regards</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly it's hard for me to hive feedback when I don't yet own the books with psionics in them. I have a hard time envisioning how it would turn out in play. Am I correct to assume that Psi score and Mode are separate stats that you start with and can level up? In that case it cn flow a lot easier as would a normal mage game. Using this system do you have an example of how a mage could cast a spell with spell factors, yantras, mudras and all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T15:35:51-07:00","id":1300967,"title":"","content":"Aptitudes are themes or categories of powers like Biokinesis, Electrokinesis, Psychokinesis, Telepathy, Vitakiensis, etc<br /> <br /> Each aptitude has 3 modes, each focused on a specific aspect of the aptitude. In first edition pychokinesis had Cryokinesis (cold), Pyrokinesis (heat) , and Telekinesis (force). Modes are from 1-5 maybe 1-6<br /> <br /> Psi Rating is your overall strength in Psychic power (the closest comparison would be the CoD supernatural stats like Blood Potency, Gnosis, Primal Urge)? PSI ranges from 2-7.<br /> <br /> I am going from memory right now. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 03-29-2019, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T12:23:45-07:00","id":1313541,"title":"","content":"How has this been going for you? Any updates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T23:12:44-07:00","id":1332500,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to post an update. After many months of long hours and real life work I was able to return and focus on this project a bit.<br /> <br /> Please see the linked files.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CeCdGWUxZ-gJfxhHTCaOp2plkt0CvcIR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">First Storypath Vampire the Requiem Character</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/12dTKqFrqqIuIBZCkheuyuH5FcwFmx-9t/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Storypath Character Creation with Splat Templates</a><br /> <br /> Both files are rough drafts and works in progress.<br /> There are items not let set, items being waffled over, so on and so forth.<br /> Integrity, Humanity, Harmony, Wisdom I am not ready to discard them and need to Storypath them.<br /> Your feedback is welcome.<br /> <br /> Several of my design and modification goals are:<br /> * One storypath character creation process only altered in the template section by the template and/or setting.<br /> - For example if Scions are more powerful than this can be boosted in the template section.<br /> * One storypath ruleset across all splats/setting, example Scale would be the same but used less or more in different settings.<br /> * Edges are available in all settings<br /> * A system that cross back and forth between CoD (VtR,MtA, CtL, WtF), EX3 and Storypath,<br /> * Keep modify only the things from the non-Storypath systems/setting that feel absolutely needed.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 08-25-2019, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 